WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.990
<b>Escape Limit</b>

3
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.830
All of you need to run.

4
00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.990
<b>Fabrio
Egghead</b>

5
00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.560
Evacuate the island!

6
00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.680
What are you talking
about, Sentomaru?

7
00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.640
Do you know
something we don't?

8
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.790
What's going
to happen to Egghead?

9
00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.100
What's going on here?

10
00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.350
Why did you deploy
the pacifistas?

11
00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:57.450
Years ago there was a place called Ohara,
an island of scholars that disappeared one

12
00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.840
day, wiped out.

13
00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.300
They called them fanatics.
Traitors to the government.

14
00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.180
And their punishment
was death.

15
00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:17.740
The Island of Ohara was once
home to the greatest library in the world.

16
00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.990
Its scholars attempted to decipher
the Poneglyphs, taking a glimpse into

17
00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.080
forbidden history,

18
00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.770
and the Government's
judgment was fierce.

19
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.790
They instituted a Buster Call,
leveling the island to the ground in a

20
00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.250
massive bombardment.

21
00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:36.100
The destruction was so vast that
only one young girl survived.

22
00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.730
Nico Robin.

23
00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.350
Punk has the greatest mind in the whole
world, and the World Government still

24
00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.450
chose to put him
in their crosshairs.

25
00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.500
Over and over, they've
made one thing clear.

26
00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:54.570
They will kill anyone
to bury their secrets.

27
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.950
If you don't escape, you'll end up
just like the scholars of Ohara.

28
00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.620
This island may be doomed,
but you don't have to die with it!

29
00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:16.540
C'mon, Straw Hat.

30
00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.140
Hurry!

31
00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:17.770
Hurry up.

32
00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.900
We don't have
a moment to lose!

33
00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.060
<b>Building A</b>

34
00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.310
<b>Building C Building B</b>

35
00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:33.510
Aaaaah!

36
00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:37.900
Hey!

37
00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:41.770
Ohh!

38
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.880
Hand Pistol!

39
00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.480
Gum-Gum...

40
00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.200
Yellow Lotus!

41
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:11.640
Woooaaah!

42
00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.000
Tempest Kick...

43
00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.430
Water!

44
00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.740
White thunder!

45
00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.940
One-Sword Style Draw!

46
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.340
Death... Lion Song.

47
00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.000
Uh! Wait, they're getting
up already? What gives?

48
00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.020
How many comebacks
are you gonna have?

49
00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.200
Who are you, Kaido?

50
00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.380
Our attacks are hitting,
but they're not doing anything.

51
00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.600
Now that I look,

52
00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.930
they kinda remind me
of this guy named King.

53
00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:44.640
He and I had a pretty
serious fight back in Wano.

54
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.760
Are you saying there
was a Lunarian in Kaido's crew?

55
00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.990
I wouldn't know.
But he had fire and wings.

56
00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:53.340
I see.

57
00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:56.810
Years ago, there was
a Lunarian held at Punk Hazard.

58
00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:00.510
He was used as a guinea pig
until he escaped with Kaido.

59
00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:01.770
His name was Alber.

60
00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.790
Thanks to him,
we acquired Lunarian blood,

61
00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.380
and the seraphim were
indeed augmented with it.

62
00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.290
Alright, good to know.

63
00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.970
Listen, guys, you gotta watch

64
00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.130
the flames
on their back real close.

65
00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.360
It's tricky.

66
00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.250
Wait till the fire
goes out for a sec,

67
00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.250
that's the only time
your attacks will work.

68
00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.170
They're pretty much
invincible when it's burning.

69
00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.800
Sorry. Guess I made
you waste your stamina.

70
00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:30.100
Honestly, I probably shoulda
noticed that right away.

71
00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.750
No complaints from me.

72
00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.540
'Least we found
out in time to win.

73
00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.390
They do look like King.

74
00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:43.600
Same white hair. Same brown
skin. Same black wings.

75
00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.330
And the big flames, too.

76
00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:47.200
– Seriously?!
– Huh?!

77
00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.050
And it still took you
that long to figure it out?

78
00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:57.230
Hey, Helmet Guy,
where are you going?

79
00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:58.790
To find Stella.

80
00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:02.030
There's one more
place he could be.

81
00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.390
Then go!

82
00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.830
Alright. Thank you.

83
00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:17.840
Heh. We've got places to be,
so don't get in our way. Got it?

84
00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.010
<b>Building C Building B</b>
<b>Third Floor
Building A</b>
<b>Building A</b>

85
00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:32.440
That's right. He's no child.

86
00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:29.350
Ruts!

87
00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.360
He tried to murder
my friends.

88
00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.550
He half-destroyed Edison!

89
00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.300
He's a killing machine!

90
00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.480
He's not Jinbe!
And he's not cute at all!

91
00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.200
We got this, Nami!
Don't hesitate!

92
00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:48.700
I'll take care of him!

93
00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.180
Just let me rip!

94
00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.590
Keep your eyes closed,
if you have to!

95
00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.720
Lightning Blast!

96
00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.030
It's not enough!

97
00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.040
Then here's some more!

98
00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.340
I got you!

99
00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.680
Sorry, Little Jinbe.

100
00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:28.760
Oh, no. He dove down
again! Run for it!

101
00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:32.770
Watch out! He's
coming from below!

102
00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:34.100
What?

103
00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.360
But I beat him, didn't I?

104
00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.400
The Sanji Constitution.
Article 1.

105
00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:57.010
The punishment
for upsetting Nami is death!

106
00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.340
Barg!

107
00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:05.940
The Sanji
Constitution. Article 9.

108
00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.820
The punishment
for making Nami scream is this!

109
00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.140
Raw Heat Strike!

110
00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.460
Sanji!

111
00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.050
You okay, Nami? You hurt?

112
00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.640
I'm fine, thanks.

113
00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.570
That's all that matters.
Let me take care of the rest.

114
00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.300
That was your warning,
brat! Now you're dead!

115
00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:47.030
Nami showed mercy,
but I'm not so kind!

116
00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:52.480
You're looking at your executioner,
Jinbe Junior!

117
00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:52.910
<b>Building A</b>

118
00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:53.030
<b>Building C Building B</b>

119
00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:53.160
<b>Building C</b>

120
00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.190
I can't believe you
turned York into stone,

121
00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.190
you backstabbing little snot!

122
00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:58.280
What can we do?

123
00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.610
They're like
specially engineered

124
00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.660
to destroy people, right?

125
00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.720
My Bubble Gun
can handle this easy!

126
00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:09.440
Really? That didn't work at all!

127
00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.220
Ha! You thought
you had me, huh?

128
00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:27.330
The bubbles from this gun
have a secret ingredient.

129
00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.930
They're instilled
with the energy of the sea!

130
00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:31.680
And you've got Green Blood,

131
00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.160
which means you have
the same weakness

132
00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.160
as people who
ate a devil fruit!

133
00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.790
My bubbles aren't so
harmless now, are they?

134
00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.510
Yeah! You are a genius!
Nice work!

135
00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.750
Yeah, obviously! C'mon!

136
00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.660
Franky! Restrain
her while we have the chance!

137
00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.380
You got it, bro!

138
00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:56.340
Ah!

139
00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.990
Don't touch me!

140
00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:05.540
You insolent boor!
Bow before me!

141
00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:07.790
Looks like your bubble
thing wore off fast.

142
00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.130
Yeah, that's 'cause
the bubble only grazed her.

143
00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.330
It's gotta stick
for the effect to last!

144
00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:16.590
You stink! You're a meanie,
meanie, meanie, meanie!

145
00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:21.270
Gah! She's angry!

146
00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.460
Hm?

147
00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:25.790
We gotta go! She's about
to shoot a laser! Move!

148
00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:28.500
Okay! Let's book it!

149
00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:32.040
No,
S-Snake! Please, don't do it!

150
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.500
You are gonna get one hell
of a time out for this, young lady!

151
00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:52.140
You let your guard down!

152
00:11:56.210 --> 00:12:00.720
Nap time! Now sit
your sassy ass down, princess!

153
00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.590
You're a genius, too, Franky!

154
00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.320
I told you! The bubbles work!

155
00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:13.260
Play nice, kid! It's over!

156
00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:16.870
It hurts. I'm dying.

157
00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:20.250
Ah! Sorry! Sorry!

158
00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:23.080
Perfume Femur!

159
00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:26.700
Gah! No, I'm turning to stone!

160
00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:28.740
She got me!

161
00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:33.500
Oh, no! Franky!

162
00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:37.680
I'll be next! We're done for!

163
00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:41.510
Ah! Here she comes!

164
00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:42.710
Stay back!

165
00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:43.620
No!

166
00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:51.010
No! No! No! No!

167
00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:01.270
Help love me!

168
00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.540
Those are Lilith!

169
00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:23.320
<b>The Old Devil Fruit
Research Lab
Underground</b>

170
00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:29.190
We searched for Stella
in every wing of the lab.

171
00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:32.890
If he's not
in this room, then...

172
00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.830
Who are you?

173
00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.910
Did you do this?
Did you put us in here?

174
00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:39.160
It can't be.

175
00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.310
You must be the missing
Cipher Pol agents!

176
00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:42.960
What happened?
Why are you here?

177
00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:43.790
Help us.

178
00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:46.600
Please! You
have to get us out of here!

179
00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:48.160
We don't wanna die!

180
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.710
We're
gonna starve.

181
00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.190
Stella!

182
00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.510
Thank
goodness you're safe.

183
00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:04.910
Huh?

184
00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:06.830
Who did this to you?

185
00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:08.800
Oh, Shaka.

186
00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:10.650
Shaka
finds Vegapunk,

187
00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.830
but before he can free
him, tragedy strikes.

188
00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.330
I'm getting
you out of here.

189
00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.220
I'll unlock the tank,
just hold on.

190
00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:18.880
Wait.

191
00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:22.130
Shaka, who came
here with you?

192
00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.510
What?

193
00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:41.180
Shaka!

194
00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.960
What just happened?

195
00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.580
He's been shot!

196
00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:10.810
<b>Saint Jaygarcia Saturn
Five Elders</b>

197
00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.370
Let's keep
our guard up, shall we?

198
00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:14.250
Yes, sir!

199
00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:19.110
<b>Future Island, Egghead</b>

200
00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.570
<b>Laboratory
Future Island, Egghead</b>

201
00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.030
<b>Building A</b>

202
00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.240
<b>Building C Building B</b>

203
00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:24.280
<b>Building B</b>

204
00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:28.120
<b>Second Floor, Building B
Laboratory</b>

205
00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.400
What?
Uncle Kizaru is coming?

206
00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:30.110
And soon. He's
commanding an entire fleet.

207
00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.450
They should be closing
in on Egghead as we speak,

208
00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.220
with over 100 ships.

209
00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.240
That's a bit excessive, isn't it?

210
00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:39.480
CP0's mission was
to assassinate Dr. Vegapunk.

211
00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.870
After that, we were
told to wait for Kizaru.

212
00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:47.550
<b>Fabriophase Factory</b>

213
00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:44.750
This is the firmest stance
they could possibly take.

214
00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:45.850
If they're sending an admiral,

215
00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:47.850
then they're not taking
any chances.

216
00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:49.550
Yes, apparently,
they're taking this

217
00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.710
even more seriously
than Ohara.

218
00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:52.710
But why?

219
00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.340
Because Dr.
Vegapunk did more

220
00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:57.310
than just uncover what Ohara
had already researched.

221
00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:01.350
Much more. He expanded
on their findings.

222
00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:05.310
Additionally, Egghead is armed
with advanced weaponry,

223
00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.280
something that Ohara lacked.

224
00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.890
You mean
the seraphim and other pacifistas?

225
00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.300
That alone is reason enough
to send a massive force.

226
00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:16.060
They would need an admiral.

227
00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.570
Contact me as
soon as anything happens!

228
00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:22.020
All communication devices
in the Labophase are inoperative.

229
00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:23.060
Understood.

230
00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.640
Cu-lick.

231
00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:27.830
Did you hear that?

232
00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.440
One look at history
will show you

233
00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:32.320
exactly what
the Navy has planned.

234
00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.960
But that can't be! You
really think they'll kill us all?

235
00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.470
They'll burn Egghead
to the ground?

236
00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:39.460
That's right! Which means
there's no time to feel sorry!

237
00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:43.830
You need to get off this island
as quickly as possible! Hurry!

238
00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:48.960
Ready the ships! Let's just
hope we have enough!

239
00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.360
But the Navy's
almost here, right?

240
00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:52.730
Sentomaru says
there's no time!

241
00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:54.750
Usopp!

242
00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:55.660
Lilith!

243
00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:59.120
<b>Third Floor, Building C
Laboratory</b>

244
00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.560
Unpetrify me right now!

245
00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.830
So what if you got my right
side? My left arm's loaded!

246
00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:06.760
You think I won't
mess you up?

247
00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:10.330
I have a Weapons Left here,
and it's got your name on it!

248
00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:11.850
But I'm a nice guy, see!

249
00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:13.990
Surrender now
and I'll let you off!

250
00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:17.750
Huh?

251
00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:19.960
I-I was just, uh...

252
00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.700
Hey!
Are you listenin'?

253
00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:27.270
I swear I'll shoot
if you don't stop!

254
00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:30.280
I just want
to know why, S-Snake!

255
00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:32.340
Whose orders are
you following?

256
00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:34.950
Why won't you listen
to a word we say?

257
00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:38.150
No!
Please, don't!

258
00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:39.930
Stop it!

259
00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:45.790
Pythagoras!

260
00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:55.230
Hey!
Wait! Get back here!

261
00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.010
<b>Building A</b>

262
00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.140
<b>Building C Building B</b>

263
00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:01.940
<b>Second Floor, Building A
Laboratory</b>

264
00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:04.330
I hope everyone else is okay.

265
00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.050
They're strong,
but we've been hearing

266
00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:08.540
an awful lot of explosions
and screams.

267
00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.340
The seraphim are
running wild out there.

268
00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:11.420
We need to hurry.

269
00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:14.270
Ah!
It doesn't make sense!

270
00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:17.960
The seraphim were helping us
and then they all went crazy!

271
00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:19.990
In that case,
perhaps they received

272
00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.700
a new command
from someone else.

273
00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:25.720
Should we find Nami?
I'm worried.

274
00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:26.950
She'll be fine.

275
00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.460
I'm sure Sanji
heard her scream,

276
00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.410
which means he'll come
running straight to her side.

277
00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:32.540
Oh! Good point!

278
00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:38.760
Anyone stuck fighting
can't continue the search.

279
00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:41.550
But we've been fortunate enough
not to run into any trouble,

280
00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:44.830
so our focus should be finding
Vegapunk, just as planned.

281
00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.960
You're right. Let's get going!

282
00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:48.040
Hold up a second.

283
00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:50.370
There's a room we haven't used
in a while that's sealed off,

284
00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:53.110
so it doesn't have
a video feed.

285
00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.390
Doesn't make sense, though.

286
00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.270
There's not much
reason to go there.

287
00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.860
It's worth a shot.
We have no leads,

288
00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:01.620
so that's still better than
wandering around blindly.

289
00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.500
Show us the way
and we'll follow.

290
00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.380
No problem!

291
00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.920
<b>Third Floor, Building A
Laboratory</b>

292
00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:16.890
Edison? Wake up!

293
00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:19.400
Edison!

294
00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:20.310
I'm leaving.

295
00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.140
For now, watch
over my old bones

296
00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:25.350
and I'll search for Vegapunk
in my spirit form!

297
00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.480
Thanks.

298
00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:30.410
Huh?

299
00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:33.150
Oh, no!

300
00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:42.860
Huh?

301
00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:49.950
Nice save, Sanji!

302
00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:57.960
Sorry, kid. This is
the power of love.

303
00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.720
It can't be beat!

304
00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:10.480
Gum-Gum...
Red Hawk!

305
00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:17.520
What a pain. Their flames
still haven't gone out yet.

306
00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:20.020
But we're wasting
energy fighting back.

307
00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:24.780
Hey!
While we were talking

308
00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.530
the Hawkeye kid ran away!

309
00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.110
Why
would he do that?

310
00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:30.820
Must have changed
their target priority.

311
00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.980
They realized we're
holding them up.

312
00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:35.460
They'll kill the weaker
targets first.

313
00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.850
It functions as
a psychological attack, too.

314
00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:41.700
If your friends are killed,
then your resolve may crumble.

315
00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.380
Luffy. Don't worry.
I'll hunt him down!

316
00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:46.100
Alright, good luck!

317
00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:49.900
Aw, crap! Hey, Usopp!
Could you go with him?

318
00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.540
If he's alone, then
he'll get lost for sure!

319
00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:57.030
Why is he so high maintenance?
Get back here, Roronoa!

320
00:20:57.030 --> 00:21:00.070
Hey, wait! Did you
just call me "Usopp"?

321
00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:12.120
This is our fight, let them go.

322
00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.880
I'll just keep punching you!

323
00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.680
Gum-Gum Hawk Gatling!

324
00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:25.260
Come on, fire, go out!

325
00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:28.180
Damn it, Straw Hat,
wait! Think this through!

326
00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:31.600
If you could punch the fire out,
we would've won already!

327
00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:36.090
These
are the events

328
00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:38.840
that would lead
to the Egghead Incident.

329
00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:41.800
A tale that would shock
the world to its core.

330
00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:45.520
But in truth,
it all started three months earlier.

331
00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:50.500
Sacred Mary Geoise,
three months ago.

332
00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:50.580
<b>The Holy Land, Mary Geoise
Three Months Ago</b>

333
00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:00.410
I can't hear you!

334
00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:04.000
I repeat,
this is Egghead.

335
00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:06.540
I need to talk
to the higher-ups.

336
00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:08.720
And what do
you want from them?

337
00:22:09.110 --> 00:22:11.110
I need to talk
to the higher-ups.

338
00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:12.800
I said,
what do you want?

339
00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:15.510
It's news
about Dr. Vegapunk.

340
00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:18.340
He's researching the Hundred
Year Void in history.

341
00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:33.040
Upon
receiving that tip,

342
00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:37.120
CP5 was dispatched to Egghead
to question Dr. Vegapunk

343
00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:39.260
and attempt
to ascertain the truth.

344
00:22:39.510 --> 00:22:42.050
However, they
found no evidence.

345
00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:44.280
After completing
the investigation,

346
00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:45.870
the agents left on their ship,

347
00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:48.790
but mysteriously vanished
on their way back.

348
00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:57.440
In light of these
strange circumstances,

349
00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:01.410
first CP7, then CP8 were
dispatched to Egghead,

350
00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:04.490
but just like CP5 before
them, they found nothing,

351
00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:06.790
and disappeared
without a trace.

352
00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.950
This is Egghead.

353
00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:13.460
Put me through
to the higher-ups.

354
00:23:23.850 --> 00:23:24.930
Later,
there was a meeting

355
00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:26.510
between the Five Elders.

356
00:23:26.510 --> 00:23:28.470
They spoke
to an outside figure,

357
00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:32.440
whose incriminating evidence
would seal Dr. Vegapunk's fate.

358
00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:34.570
The betrayal was complete.

359
00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:36.720
Cu-lick.

360
00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:38.200
The Five
Elders decided

361
00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:41.950
that Dr. Vegapunk
must be assassinated.

362
00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:45.620
Cipher
Pol "Aigis" Zero

363
00:23:45.620 --> 00:23:48.820
was tasked with that
mission, and set sail.

364
00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:52.190
However, they feared a deadly
retaliation from Vegapunk,

365
00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:53.130
so one of the Five Elders

366
00:23:53.130 --> 00:23:55.740
decided to go
to Egghead in person.

367
00:23:56.410 --> 00:23:59.610
He chose Admiral
Kizaru as his escort.

368
00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:05.630
Cu-lick.

369
00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:07.100
Taking
every precaution,

370
00:24:07.100 --> 00:24:09.220
they also requested
reinforcements

371
00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:12.350
from a series
of Navy outposts.

372
00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:17.830
Together,
they formed a fleet.

373
00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:21.060
It was a deployment
befitting a full-scale war.

374
00:24:35.410 --> 00:24:37.370
However,
an unexpected guest

375
00:24:37.370 --> 00:24:38.780
showed up first.

376
00:24:38.970 --> 00:24:43.060
The newly crowned Emperor
of the Sea, Straw Hat Luffy.

377
00:24:54.760 --> 00:24:57.210
Already
facing a difficult operation,

378
00:24:57.210 --> 00:24:59.010
the Government feared
that the Straw Hats

379
00:24:59.170 --> 00:25:01.050
would throw
everything into chaos.

380
00:25:01.130 --> 00:25:02.160
See this?

381
00:25:02.710 --> 00:25:03.790
You give people an inch

382
00:25:03.790 --> 00:25:06.030
and they give you
nothin' but a headache.

383
00:25:11.170 --> 00:25:12.670
It's them again!

384
00:25:13.950 --> 00:25:15.120
For better or worse,

385
00:25:15.120 --> 00:25:20.620
the incident will come
to a conclusion in only a day's time.

386
00:25:20.760 --> 00:25:23.470
But the aftermath may
very well reshape the future

387
00:25:23.640 --> 00:25:26.060
of the entire world.

388
00:25:27.170 --> 00:25:34.140
<b>The Old Devil Fruit
Research Lab
Underground</b>

389
00:25:28.850 --> 00:25:30.570
Is
this your doing?

390
00:25:30.650 --> 00:25:33.060
All this chaos
and destruction?

391
00:25:33.470 --> 00:25:34.410
Answer me!

392
00:25:41.920 --> 00:25:42.720
The...

393
00:26:08.770 --> 00:26:10.540
Why are you doing this?

394
00:26:11.630 --> 00:26:13.190
Why, York?

395
00:26:19.280 --> 00:26:20.840
What do you mean, "why"?

396
00:26:20.920 --> 00:26:24.140
When this is done,
I'll be a Celestial Dragon.

397
00:26:24.180 --> 00:26:28.090
Huh? What are you
talking about, York?

398
00:26:28.090 --> 00:26:30.340
You've been to Mary Geoise,
haven't you?

399
00:26:30.340 --> 00:26:33.300
Why would you want to associate
with leeches like them?

400
00:26:33.590 --> 00:26:37.670
Ha-ha! You
sound just like Shaka.

401
00:26:37.780 --> 00:26:39.900
Well, before he ate lead.

402
00:26:39.980 --> 00:26:45.860
I never understood
having so many of us.

403
00:26:47.220 --> 00:26:51.140
Seven Doctor Vegapunks
is a bit much.

404
00:26:52.900 --> 00:26:54.780
I think one
would be plenty.
